# Phase 18 offset request header compatibility and current-revision P18-V02 gate — 2026-10-17T21:37:56Z

- Branch: `phase/19-phase-18-compatibility-release-gate`.
- Implementation commit: `607be744 fix(protocol): match Java offset request header decoding`.
- Java behavior oracle: RocketMQ client 5.5.1 source commit
  `efa1be59d6fc747ad220f036c86030f05f0419f9`; the external Java checkout was
  read-only and was not used as a substitute for the pinned revision.
- Scope: the four offset-boundary request headers now preserve Java's nullable
  topic/boxed numeric fields under both `useFastEncode` hints, including the
  inherited `lo` field. Search header behavior also covers nullable timestamp
  and boundary type, `liteTopic`, and the Java getter's `LOWER` fallback; max
  offset `committed` retains the primitive `true` default and Java boolean
  conversion. Call sites now handle the nullable decoded fields at their
  source-equivalent owner boundary.
- Added invoked Java and Rust fixtures for absent, valid, and malformed input
  under both decode hints. Fixture SHA-256:
  `f6cf1cc07b0f9c0c3263f7210393595cfb0c8898257dfdd3fc81f39afebe71a3`.
- Updated the Phase 9 header coverage and method matrices and the Java 5.5.1
  compatibility record. No plan file changed.

## Current-revision server-free verification

- On `rust:1.85.0-bookworm`, Linux ARM64, standard Docker bridge, with
  `--test-threads=1`: `cargo test --workspace --locked --offline` PASS and
  `cargo test --workspace --all-features --locked --offline` PASS. The focused
  offset-boundary header tests and header validation matrix passed as part of
  both full runs.
- `cargo check --workspace --all-targets --all-features --locked --offline`:
  PASS.
- `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets --all-features --locked --offline --
  -D warnings`: PASS.
- `TZ=UTC mvn -o -q -f compat/java-reference/pom.xml verify`: PASS; all 37
  scenario rows, Java fixture drift checks, and Rust/Java cross-decodes passed.
- `python3 tests/differential/compare.py --self-test` and
  `python3 tests/differential/compare.py --validate-manifest`: PASS; 37 rows.
- `bash tests/stress/run-offline-smoke.sh`: PASS; 16 deterministic race/leak
  cases × 3 repetitions. `fuzz_smoke`: PASS; 105 frame seeds, 11 message
  seeds, 1,856 bounded mutations, 146 frame decodes, and 113 message decodes.
- Release examples built; `cargo bench --workspace --no-run --locked --offline`
  compiled all workspace benchmarks. The offline benchmark ran on Linux ARM64,
  Rust 1.85.0: frame encode/decode 1,228.9 ns, Zstandard message decode
  725.0 ns, Producer request construction 938.7 ns, 128-entry route lookup
  14.5 ns, pending completion 6,148.9 ns. Allocation observations were 4,676;
  197,493; 3,665; 0; and 9,530 bytes per iteration respectively. These are
  observations, not acceptance thresholds.
- `cargo metadata --locked --format-version 1 --no-deps`, workspace metadata
  and dependency-direction check, and `cargo package --workspace --list
  --locked --allow-dirty`: PASS. Package listings contain LICENSE and NOTICE.
  `cargo fmt --all -- --check` and `git diff --check`: PASS.
- The first macOS workspace test process stalled in `_dyld_start` before
  entering its test binary and was interrupted. A first Linux container run
  with `--network none` failed host-address and signal-selection tests because
  it lacked a normal container interface; the standard-bridge full default and
  all-feature runs then passed. No code failure reproduced.

